{"title":"2023 IOQM/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IOQM/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For any finite non empty set X of integers, let max(X) denote the largest element\nof X and |X| denote the number of elements in X . If N is the number of ordered\npairs (A, B) of finite non-empty sets of positive integers, such that\nmax(A) × |B| = 12; and\n|A| × max(B) = 11\nand N can be written as 100a + b where a, b are positive integers less than 100,\nfind a + b .\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IOQM/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The condition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/5/9b5c7f453f434fd6bafd1732f739c69f87d92458.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|A| \\times \\text{max}(B) = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"150\" height=\"20\" /> gives us two cases:\n</p><p><br />\nCASE 1:  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/9/ad9150c8e7418fbc2e52a8a06c11cbd6cb6222bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|A| = 1,\\ \\text{max}(B) = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"175\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>The condition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/e/a4e84c4fcea87bd2fb45cd8c737c65160229a7f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{max}(A) \\times |B| = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"150\" height=\"20\" /> gives us several subcases:\n</p><p><br />\nSUBCASE I: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/0/e80c504aefda3833c0c3897c360e027fa2424184.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{max}(A) = 12,\\ |B| = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"175\" height=\"20\" /> \n</p><p>Notice that, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/1/ae15a75d4a8347a8316abdc34a43a61f6ee0020e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=\\text{max}(A), r=|A|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"165\" height=\"20\" />, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d118210c0fb7a9c1a0c3e092eaa5bea915d7e75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$^{m-1}C_{r-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"69\" height=\"21\" /> ways to choose the remaining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/4/9d42de090a4ce87ba386a02de55516af64691404.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" /> distinct elements from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/7/057090d565372204a43c5ccf197f32af8cc311dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,\\dots,m-1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"117\" height=\"20\" />, i.e. there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d118210c0fb7a9c1a0c3e092eaa5bea915d7e75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$^{m-1}C_{r-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"69\" height=\"21\" /> possible sets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Hence, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/3/5e39c775b56e5ac03edba626fef7c446a189d2f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$^{12-1}C_{1-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"21\" /> possibilities for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/a/a1af941979b9ae6907a2c6c5dae7db68019e5a28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$^{11-1}C_{1-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"21\" /> possibilities for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/9/bb9e9d754b317eedf8127c0fa37eb9cf39d9fd83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$^{12-1}C_{1-1} \\cdot ^{11-1}C_{1-1} = ^{11}C_{0} \\cdot ^{10}C_{0} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"292\" height=\"21\" /> total possibilities for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/0/bb0c75d9abe3e693ba0bb677cecbb923cefd81af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A,B)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nSUBCASE II: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/0/d00677eec522ef73e63aff8840c598f2095a2a88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{max}(A) = 6,\\ |B| = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"166\" height=\"20\" /> \n</p><p>Similarly, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/c/34c9ebbdef177ec4de91fd4634fb3ba16b899b21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$^{5}C_{0} \\cdot ^{10}C_{1} = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"20\" /> possibilities for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/0/bb0c75d9abe3e693ba0bb677cecbb923cefd81af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A,B)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nSUBCASE III: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/2/eb251b8408fd51344234c9654ad75a24f15a56c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{max}(A) = 4,\\ |B| = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"166\" height=\"20\" /> \n</p><p>Similarly, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/5/2e50d2160b4a7799496f48277f82f2285d5a7396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$^{3}C_{0} \\cdot ^{10}C_{2} = 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"20\" /> possibilities for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/0/bb0c75d9abe3e693ba0bb677cecbb923cefd81af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A,B)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nSUBCASE IV: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/2/7028d391592cda01b2b8840944a91948dab0c5c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{max}(A) = 3,\\ |B| = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"166\" height=\"20\" /> \n</p><p>Similarly, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/1/5911695bdc3bbe73681531764a3a160c92d5badb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$^{2}C_{0} \\cdot ^{10}C_{3} = 120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"129\" height=\"20\" /> possibilities for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/0/bb0c75d9abe3e693ba0bb677cecbb923cefd81af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A,B)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nSUBCASE V: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/a/aca25b56935512beb4f1df3e263b4093dfa41c09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{max}(A) = 2,\\ |B| = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"166\" height=\"20\" /> \n</p><p>Similarly, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/9/e695746d769c4aaa6bf13a6aa294c30f8614a901.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$^{1}C_{0} \\cdot ^{10}C_{5} = 252$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"129\" height=\"20\" /> possibilities for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/0/bb0c75d9abe3e693ba0bb677cecbb923cefd81af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A,B)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nSUBCASE VI: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/b/2ebafc37531ac8de2edb1219d4aef5aca6bfe285.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{max}(A) = 1,\\ |B| = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"175\" height=\"20\" /> \n</p><p>Note that it is impossible to choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/572ac27aab1a8abd8d9b533fafc987065820636b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12-1=11$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"90\" height=\"12\" /> elements from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/c/8fcdd5bc25c4fb4ed3a6f1000bead98595d4d67f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 - 1=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> options, hence there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possibilities for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/0/bb0c75d9abe3e693ba0bb677cecbb923cefd81af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A,B)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nTotal number of possibilities for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/5/af5364d125389949f26fa235813321b4dfa6b23e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A,B) = 1 + 10 + 45 + 120 + 252 + 0 = 428$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"348\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><br />\nCASE 2:  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/5/485d7cecee13e01abacb900d28179072446a2888.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|A| = 11,\\ \\text{max}(B) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"175\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/0/570f36fd1393f81d9fcc29020377ebb6776f3fe7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{max}(A) \\geq |A| = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"151\" height=\"20\" /> must hold true, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/0/e80c504aefda3833c0c3897c360e027fa2424184.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{max}(A) = 12,\\ |B| = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"175\" height=\"20\" /> is the only possibility, yielding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/d/dddf496865d1c7c1cb7fe115fd3916f398f9b654.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$^{11}C_{10} \\cdot ^{0}C_{0} = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"20\" /> total possibilities for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/0/bb0c75d9abe3e693ba0bb677cecbb923cefd81af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A,B)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p><br />\nAs there is no overcounting, the total number of possibilities for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/9/da9c8a50078f897bbb2f4e43a528abb8a4d535cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A,B) = 428 + 11 = 439 = 100 \\cdot 4 + 39$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"310\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/3/9b387acf64e69c15a07eb01b102b7be0bc6ef725.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 + 39 = \\boxed{43}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"105\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~biggest_glitter_hater\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018065058\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.016 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.027 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 128/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7801/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:25556:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018065058 and revision id 290688. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}